UID:dp-curator-support-open-call-2027@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T190725Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Deadline: 2027 d/p Curator Support Open Call (Seoul)
DESCRIPTION:d/p is an independent alternative exhibition space in the Nakwo
 n Arcade\, the historic mixed-use commercial and residential complex in Jo
 ngno-gu\, Seoul built in 1968. Its Curator Support programme\, sponsored b
 y NakwonSangga\, has selected two to three independent curators every year
  since 2018\, giving each an exhibition venue\, curatorial collaboration w
 ith the d/p team\, and a modest curatorial grant to develop and realise th
 eir curatorial practice. ELIGIBILITY: individual curators or teams with at
  least one curating experience within the past three years. The applying c
 urator or team cannot participate in the exhibition as an artist\; curator
 s and artists must be clearly distinguished. SELECTION: approximately two 
 individuals or teams. WHAT IS PROVIDED: a curatorial grant of KRW 4\,000\,
 000 including tax\; use of the d/p exhibition space of approximately 187 s
 quare metres\; and a five-week exhibition slot somewhere between March and
  December 2027\, with installation and deinstallation time counted separat
 ely from the five weeks. PROCESS: first round is a document review of the 
 APPLICATION and PROPOSAL submitted in the provided format\; second round i
 s individual interviews followed by final selection. Interviews are conduc
 ted offline in principle\, but may be held online if the applicant is abro
 ad or in other exceptional circumstances. HOW TO APPLY: submit the APPLICA
 TION via the Google Form and the PROPOSAL by email to dslashp@gmail.com be
 tween 3 August and 30 September 2026. The proposal template is downloadabl
 e from the link in the @dslashp Instagram bio. File name format: '2027 d/p
  Curator Support Application_Applicant Name'. Submit as PDF\; if the propo
 sal includes video\, provide a link rather than a file. KEY DATES: submiss
 ions 3 August to 30 September 2026\; first round results announced in the 
 first week of October 2026 by individual contact\; second round interviews
  in the second week of October 2026\; final selection announced in the thi
 rd week of October 2026 by individual contact and on the @dslashp account.
  Inquiries: Minji Lee\, Curator\, dslashp@gmail.com.\n\nOrganisation: d/p\
 , sponsored by NakwonSangga\nLocation: d/p\, 417 Nakwon Arcade\, 428 Samil
 -daero\, Jongno-gu\, Seoul\, South Korea. Interviews are held offline in p
 rinciple\, with online interviews possible for applicants abroad or in oth
 er exceptional circumstances.\nAward: Curatorial grant of KRW 4\,000\,000 
 (including tax) per selected curator or team\, plus use of d/p's approxima
 tely 187 square metre exhibition space for a five-week exhibition and cura
 torial collaboration with the d/p team. Approximately two curators or team
 s are selected. No application fee.\nDuration: Five-week exhibition slot b
 etween March and December 2027\, with installation and deinstallation peri
 ods separate\n\nMore: https://docs.google.com/forms/d/1iSjEuCjay7DhL1AF1NC
 ePu-5RV3t_10WT0CNcjNNJy8/preview?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm
 _medium=referral
URL:https://docs.google.com/forms/d/1iSjEuCjay7DhL1AF1NCePu-5RV3t_10WT0CNcj
 NNJy8/preview?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:d/p\, 417 Nakwon Arcade\, 428 Samil-daero\, Jongno-gu\, Seoul\, So
 uth Korea. Interviews are held offline in principle\, with online intervie
 ws possible for applicants abroad or in other exceptional circumstances.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:this-is-gender-regional-curatorial-fellowship-2026@artificialnouveau.gi
 thub.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T190725Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260922
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260923
SUMMARY:Deadline: This is Gender Regional Curatorial Fellowship 2026
DESCRIPTION:This is Gender\, the photography and visual culture platform ru
 n by Global 50/50\, is launching its inaugural Regional Curatorial Fellows
  Programme for early-career curators and cultural practitioners working ac
 ross photography\, visual culture and gender justice. The premise: images 
 shape how gender\, power and social realities are understood\, feeding pub
 lic debate\, cultural memory\, research\, advocacy and policy\, yet the co
 mmunities and visual practices that should inform those narratives stay un
 derrepresented in the institutions that circulate them. The programme's ar
 gument is that diversifying who makes images is not enough\, and that it a
 lso matters who selects\, contextualises\, writes about\, commissions and 
 circulates them. For the first time\, This is Gender is embedding regional
  curators directly inside its global photography competition\, which has r
 un six cycles and receives thousands of submissions a year. WHAT THE FELLO
 WSHIP INVOLVES: working inside the competition and seeing first-hand how a
  major platform discovers\, reviews and champions new work\; shaping curat
 orial decisions by bringing regional knowledge and cultural insight into t
 he selection and interpretation of work\; contributing to public-facing pr
 ojects including exhibitions\, editorial outputs and digital storytelling 
 while developing your own writing\, framing and curatorial voice\; direct 
 engagement with international judges\, curators\, artists\, editors and cu
 ltural practitioners\; and building a network across an international coho
 rt of peers. WHO SHOULD APPLY: curators\, critics\, writers\, researchers\
 , artistic directors\, photographers\, organisers and cultural practitione
 rs from global majority countries and historically underrepresented commun
 ities. Early-career practitioners and recent graduates are strongly encour
 aged\, and a formal curatorial title is not required. HOW TO APPLY: read t
 he full role description and FAQs on the fellowship page and submit the on
 line application form\; the organisers offer the application in alternativ
 e formats and are open to a conversation before applying. Applications clo
 se 22 September 2026.\n\nOrganisation: This is Gender (Global 50/50)\nLoca
 tion: Remote and part-time\, working within a global photography competiti
 on. Applications are invited from practitioners in global majority countri
 es and historically underrepresented communities\, including Asia\, Africa
 \, Latin America\, the Middle East\, Oceania\, and diasporic communities w
 orldwide.\nAward: Stipend of up to GBP 3\,000 for the seven-month part-tim
 e fellowship. No application fee.\nDuration: Seven months from October 202
 6\, part-time and flexible\n\nMore: https://thisisgender.global5050.org/re
 gional-curatorial-fellowship/?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_me
 dium=referral
URL:https://thisisgender.global5050.org/regional-curatorial-fellowship/?utm
 _source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Remote and part-time\, working within a global photography competi
 tion. Applications are invited from practitioners in global majority count
 ries and historically underrepresented communities\, including Asia\, Afri
 ca\, Latin America\, the Middle East\, Oceania\, and diasporic communities
  worldwide.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:cultural-horizons-residencies-subgrants-2027@artificialnouveau.github.i
 o
DTSTAMP:20260901T190725Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Deadline: Cultural Horizons Residencies: Subgrants for EU-Ukrainian
  Residency Projects 2027
DESCRIPTION:Cultural Horizons strengthens the cultural sector in Ukraine by
  promoting joint EU-Ukrainian cultural initiatives and expanding access fo
 r Ukrainians affected by the war to cultural and artistic networks in Euro
 pe. Running 2026 to 2027\, it provides subgrants for projects developed th
 rough EU-Ukrainian partnerships and builds a Europe-wide network of cultur
 al expert mentors. THIS CALL\, the Residencies strand\, gives subgrants to
  EU-based institutions to run (a) residency placements and/or (b) educatio
 n projects organised on the basis of residencies\, for and with Ukrainian 
 artistic and cultural professionals during 2027. WHO CAN APPLY: artistic a
 nd cultural organisations and initiatives registered within the EU. Consor
 tium applications are allowed but must designate one lead organisation to 
 submit and manage the funding. This is an organisational call\, so individ
 ual Ukrainian artists cannot apply directly\; they participate as the host
 ed residents. Applicants must show they can host Ukrainian professionals i
 n 2027 and complete the project in the stated window. NGOs and public sect
 or institutions working with displaced and vulnerable groups are prioritis
 ed. CONDITIONS: applicants must confirm the absence of ties with the Russi
 an Federation\, meaning no working partnerships with Russia or Russian org
 anisations and no visits to Russian-occupied territories after 2014\, comm
 it to refrain from the glorification of Russian imperialism\, and comply w
 ith the EU sanctions regime. They must also demonstrate a commitment to di
 versity\, equity and inclusion and provide a working environment based on 
 mutual trust\, awareness and intercultural sensitivity. WHO THE MONEY IS M
 EANT TO REACH: Ukrainian artists and cultural practitioners\, whether inde
 pendent or employed\, including early-career specialists\, debut artists\,
  cultural managers\, researchers\, analysts and conservators\; vulnerable 
 groups from Ukraine including internally displaced persons\, young artists
 \, and communities in frontline and conflict-affected areas\; and cultural
  organisations in Ukraine\, with particular focus on small communities\, l
 ocal initiatives\, independent cultural spaces and NGOs. APPLYING: submiss
 ion is through a JotForm hosted by Cultural Vistas and must be complete\, 
 including uploads\, or it will not be processed. You should receive an ema
 il confirmation\; if it does not arrive\, the submission was not received.
  Enquiries to culturalhorizons@culturalvistas.eu. NOTE ON DATES: the eligi
 bility section says projects must be completed within January to August 20
 27 while the application instructions give the implementation phase as 1 J
 anuary to 30 July 2027\, so plan to the earlier end date. Programme backgr
 ound is at culturalvistas.eu under Our Programs\, Professional Study Tours
 \, Cultural Horizons.\n\nOrganisation: Ukrainian Cultural Foundation and C
 ultural Vistas\, funded by the Creative Europe programme of the European U
 nion\nLocation: Applicant organisations must be registered in the EU. Resi
 dencies are hosted in the EU for Ukrainian artistic and cultural professio
 nals.\nAward: EUR 5\,000 to 20\,000 per subgrant\, with a minimum of 20 su
 bgrants to be awarded. No application fee.\nDuration: Projects run between
  1 January and 30 July 2027\, minimum 3 months and maximum 8 months. Appli
 cations 29 June to 30 September 2026\; evaluation October to November 2026
 . Final reports are due within one month of project completion and no late
 r than 15 August 2027.\n\nMore: https://culturalvistas.jotform.com/2617534
 20662859?utm_source=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://culturalvistas.jotform.com/261753420662859?utm_source=artificia
 lnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Applicant organisations must be registered in the EU. Residencies 
 are hosted in the EU for Ukrainian artistic and cultural professionals.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:unidee-cittadellarte-visiting-research-curator-2027-28@artificialnouvea
 u.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T190725Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260913
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260914
SUMMARY:Deadline: UNIDEE Residency Programs: Visiting Research Curator 2027
 -28
DESCRIPTION:Cittadellarte is recruiting a Visiting Research Curator to shap
 e the research arc of the UNIDEE Residency Modules for 2027-2028\, the rol
 e most recently held by Nina Fiocco and Gaia Martino. Founded by Michelang
 elo Pistoletto in 1999\, the residency has hosted thousands of artists and
  cultural professionals from 52 countries. WHAT THEY WANT: rather than a f
 ixed theme set in advance\, they want a curator who brings their own line 
 of inquiry and develops it collectively through the modules. Suggested the
 matic areas are the evolving landscape of socially engaged art practices\,
  research-driven and process-oriented practice\, and the conditions of cul
 tural work and cultural workers\, aligned with UNIDEE's focus on artistic 
 research in response to ecological\, geopolitical and technological challe
 nges. They also flag a specific interest in how contemporary art practices
  are archived\, drawing on the UNIDEE archive\, which documents over two d
 ecades of socially engaged art initiatives. THIS IS A JOB\, NOT A GRANT: t
 he duties list is long and operational. It covers proposing the overarchin
 g curatorial theme\, designing and delivering a minimum of 8 weekly reside
 ntial modules per year\, writing the curatorial statement and resident ope
 n call\, recruiting mentors and guests\, selecting residents\, hosting and
  facilitating every module in person\, communications and website texts\, 
 a dissemination strategy\, and conceiving and editing publications. There 
 is also teaching-adjacent work with the Unidee Academy of Contemporary Art
 s\, including public lectures and studio visits. Budget the time before ap
 plying. PROFILE: experience curating art in the public sphere and socially
  engaged art\, specialised knowledge of international contemporary art\, e
 xperience designing experimental and collaborative educational activities\
 , and experience with artistic research and dissemination standards. Excel
 lent English required\; Italian welcome but not essential. APPLYING: onlin
 e form with a project proposal of maximum 5000 characters stating your vis
 ion for the modules programme and a development strategy including possibl
 e mentors and guests\, plus a CV\, a portfolio of maximum three relevant p
 rojects\, and TWO LETTERS OF RECOMMENDATION\, so line up your referees ear
 ly. A jury of the UNIDEE Advisory Board\, the Director of Cittadellarte an
 d invited experts decides. They do not give feedback on unsuccessful propo
 sals.\n\nOrganisation: Fondazione Pistoletto Cittadellarte and UNIDEE Resi
 dency Programs\nLocation: Cittadellarte\, Biella\, Italy. Requires in-pers
 on presence at Cittadellarte for a minimum of one month plus the full leng
 th of each module.\nAward: Compensation and contractual terms commensurate
  with the candidate's level of professional experience\, starting from a g
 ross amount of EUR 22\,000 for the appointment\, excluding travel and hosp
 itality\, which are covered separately. No application fee.\nDuration: Tem
 porary appointment from November 2026 to December 2028\, covering the 2027
 -2028 research arc and a minimum of 8 residency modules per year. Deadline
  13 September 2026 at 23:59 CEST\; shortlisted candidates interviewed onli
 ne by mid-October 2026\, with the selected candidate announced a few days 
 later.\n\nMore: https://unidee.cittadellarte.it/activity.html?id=269&utm_s
 ource=artificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://unidee.cittadellarte.it/activity.html?id=269&utm_source=artific
 ialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Cittadellarte\, Biella\, Italy. Requires in-person presence at Cit
 tadellarte for a minimum of one month plus the full length of each module.
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:sam-residencies-cycle-4-2027-2028@artificialnouveau.github.io
DTSTAMP:20260901T190725Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260930
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261001
SUMMARY:Deadline: SAM Residencies: Cycle 4 Open Call 2027/2028 (Singapore A
 rt Museum)
DESCRIPTION:Open call for Cycle 4 of the Singapore Art Museum's residency p
 rogramme\, welcoming artists\, curators\, educators\, researchers and crea
 tive practitioners worldwide\, as individuals\, duos or collectives\, from
  all mediums and disciplines. THREE STRANDS frame the cycle\, to be interp
 reted in relation to your practice: Listening/Attuning (practices respondi
 ng critically to the urgencies of our time)\, Making/Material Cultures (ma
 terial inquiry and the process of making)\, and Beyond Human/Interdependen
 ce (relationships between humans\, technologies\, ecologies and other form
 s of life). THREE TRACKS: Artist Residency for new artistic research\, exp
 erimentation and modes of making\; Community & Education Residency for pra
 ctice at the intersection of art\, education and community engagement\; an
 d Curatorial & Research Residency for new approaches to exhibition making 
 and research methodologies. SUPPORT: shared studio or co-working space\, m
 useum resources and expertise\, network building and opportunities for pub
 lic engagement\, alongside the stipend and (for international residents) f
 lights\, housing and visa help. SELECTION: an international panel of respe
 cted voices in contemporary art. APPLY via the SAM submission portal (acco
 unt required) with a CV\, portfolio\, statement of interest of 500 to 1\,0
 00 words interpreting the thematic strands\, and a character-reference rec
 ommendation submitted by the recommender through the portal. Applications 
 1 August to 30 September 2026\, 23:59 GMT+8\; residencies run June 2027 to
  December 2028.\n\nOrganisation: Singapore Art Museum (SAM)\nLocation: Sin
 gapore. Open worldwide\; international residents get housing\, flights and
  visa assistance.\nAward: Monthly stipend of SGD 1\,500 for all residents.
  International residents (1 to 3 months) additionally receive a roundtrip 
 economy flight\, a housing arrangement and assistance with visa formalitie
 s. Singapore-based residents (up to 6 months) additionally receive a month
 ly local allowance of SGD 250. Shared studio or co-working space included.
  No application fee.\nDuration: Residencies take place between June 2027 a
 nd December 2028: 1 to 3 months for international applicants\, up to 6 mon
 ths for Singapore-based applicants. Deadline 30 September 2026 at 23:59 GM
 T+8.\n\nMore: https://samresidencies.smapply.org/prog/cycle4/?utm_source=a
 rtificialnouveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
URL:https://samresidencies.smapply.org/prog/cycle4/?utm_source=artificialno
 uveaugrantdesk&utm_medium=referral
LOCATION:Singapore. Open worldwide\; international residents get housing\, 
 flights and visa assistance.
END:VEVENT
END:VCALENDAR
